{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 124, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring the missing direct input-to-output residual path gives the largest gains (+15 to +34 pp) compared with replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on an absent edge 3 adds a new information path, whereas replacing an existing op loses something."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the input-to-output skip with a conv removes the residual connection and consistently hurt all three datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, removing edge 0 disconnects nodes 1 and 2 from the input, collapsing the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 receives nothing, the node2-to-output conv carries more of the cell's useful computation, so upgrading it helps more."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 3 preserves signal at the output, so a parameter-free pool on edge 5 does little harm, unlike the large drops seen with a conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling op with a learnable conv on the first edge gave large gains across datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an identity on edge 0 with a 1x1 conv loses an easy gradient path and was strongly negative."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 1 is a pooled copy of the input, adding a 3x3 conv on node1-to-output consistently reduced accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv removes more learned capacity than deleting a pool or skip on the same edge."}], "tok": 18157, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor